{"id": "De4OapWJYKe", "title": "Video by vedastovikings", "description": "Oppenheimer quoted one line from this moment. Here is the whole scene. 🔥\n\nKurukshetra. Two armies wait. Arjuna lowers his bow and refuses to fight. Krishna smiles, teaches him, and gives him divine sight. And Arjuna sees the Universal Form: the light of a thousand suns, every god inside one body, and Time itself, with mouths of fire.\n\n“I am Time, the destroyer of worlds.” (Bhagavad Gita 11.32)\n\nEvery line on screen comes from the Gita (chapters 1, 2, 10, 11 and 18), with its verse number. One moment doesn’t: no verse says time stopped. In the text they simply speak between the two armies, just as the weapons are about to fly (1.20–21, 2.10), so we marked it on screen as a popular retelling.\n\n🎨 Every frame drawn in code\n🎵 Original score: tanpura, bansuri, sarangi, shankh, temple bells and choir\n\nSave this for Gita Jayanti 🙏 Send it to someone who needs 2.47 today.\nFollow @vedastovikings for the world’s epics, from the Vedas to the Vikings.\n\n#BhagavadGita #Krishna #Mahabharata #Vishvarupa #Kurukshetra", "channel": "vedastovikings", "uploader_id": "60997589521", "uploader": "Vedas to Vikings | Mythology films", "timestamp": 1792848462, "like_count": 2296, "comment_count": 14, "http_headers": {"User-Agent": "Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/148.0.0.0 Safari/537.36", "Accept": "text/html,application/xhtml+xml,application/xml;q=0.9,*/*;q=0.8", "Accept-Language": "en-us,en;q=0.5", "Sec-Fetch-Mode": "navigate", "Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-29805736855686101a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 60.839, "asr": 44100, "format_note": "DASH audio", "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "none", "acodec": "mp4a.40.5", "url": "https://instagram.fblr22-2.fna.fbcdn.net/o1/v/t2/f2/m78/AQPWPZ9XbtEdUs_PAvLZdTYMLGcg5FDnUYd4C2MXxq0qwgxc1pkXsKDXw9_6t5C6PrBsF9HtY39TRYy2COMG1K8zH7whtGbmEyCTz2M.mp4?_nc_cat=108&_nc_oc=AdoMcZ